  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/pseudogastromyzon-cheni-2/",
      "html": "<p>There is a lot of confusion regarding the identity of two species of Pseudogastromyzon, namely P. cheni and P. myersi. Both species look almost identical and both show a high degree of variability in coloration. There is only one known way to tell them apart for sure: taking measurements. The first measurement is the distance between the origin of the pectoral fin and the origin of the ventral fin. The second is the distance between the origin of the ventral fin and the anus. If both measurements are equal, the fish is P. myersi. If distance 1 is larger than distance 2, the fish is P. cheni. This difference can be found in both sexes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/pseudogastromyzon-cheni-2/",
      "html": "<p>They love a tank with a lot of current. The water temperature should not climb over 24°C for longer periods.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "equipment",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/pseudogastromyzon-cheni-2/",
      "html": "<p>They love a tank with a lot of current, a lot of stones and a lot of light.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/pseudogastromyzon-cheni-2/",
      "html": "<p>Like all loaches, hillstream loaches feed on small invertebrates, but the horny lips also allow them to scratch algae from the stones. In the aquarium they readily accept any usual type of fish food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/07-carp-like-fishes-1-loaches/pseudogastromyzon-cheni-2/",
      "html": "<p>Both species are very nice and very entertaining aquarium inhabitants. They are imported via Hong Kong.</p>"
    }
  ],
